# Phone navigation: top bar and nav drawer

## What to build

Below 900 px (the `NARROW` breakpoint) graph-manager's left nav (`<nav className="gm-nav">` in `apps/graph-manager/src/web/Shell.tsx`) no longer takes room on the page. Instead a 48 px top bar `<header className="gm-topbar" data-testid="gm-topbar">` shows a menu button ☰ (`data-testid="nav-menu"`, `aria-label="Open navigation"`, `aria-expanded`), the brand mark, the current page title, and a live-runs dot when runs are live. ☰ opens the existing nav, unchanged (full labels, badges, status rows, Jump to, theme, Log out), as a drawer from the left (`.gm-nav.drawer`, `width: min(300px, 86vw)`) over a scrim (`.gm-nav-scrim`, `data-testid="nav-scrim"`). The drawer closes on a nav link tap (route change), a scrim tap and Escape; focus moves into the drawer on open and back to ☰ on close. From 900 to 1099 px the 56 px icon rail stays exactly as today, from 1100 px the full nav stays as today, and the live-run-detail rail (`.gm-shell.rail`) applies only at 900 px and up. While the phone keyboard is open (`html.kb-open`, set by `ui/viewport.ts`) the top bar is hidden below 900 px. The command palette (`CommandPalette.tsx`) items stay tappable and the palette fits a phone screen.

What already exists (delivered by an earlier task, in the codebase now):
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/media.ts` exports `NARROW = "(max-width: 899.98px)"`, `PHONE`, `COARSE` and `useMedia(query: string): boolean` (a `matchMedia` hook that follows `change` events and returns `false` when `window.matchMedia` is missing, as in jsdom). Use `useMedia(NARROW)`.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/viewport.ts` exports `useVisualViewport()`, already called at the top of `Shell`. It sets `--app-h` (visual viewport height in px) on `<html>` and the class `kb-open` on `<html>` while the on-screen keyboard is open.
- `Shell.css` already uses `height: var(--app-h, 100dvh)` on `.gm-shell` with `padding: env(safe-area-inset-top) env(safe-area-inset-right) 0 env(safe-area-inset-left)`, and `.gm-main` / `.gm-nav` use `height: calc(var(--app-h, 100dvh) - env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px))`.
- `ui/base.css` has an `@media (pointer: coarse)` block giving `.nav-item`, `.status-row`, `.nav-jump`, `.palette-item`, `.nav-icon-btn`, `.nav-logout` a 40 px hit area.

Out of scope: page layouts, Terminals page changes, PWA tags, the engine's live run page.

## Context: files to read before implementing

- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/Shell.tsx` (whole file, ~220 lines) — `NavItem` (:42–53), `RUN_DETAIL` / `isLiveRunDetail` (:55–63), `Shell` (:66–219): `rail` (:70), the palette state (:74, :87), the window capture keydown listener for g-chords (:98–130; it ignores Escape and skips when `[aria-modal="true"]` exists), the nav markup (:136–214), `<main className="gm-main">` (:215), `<CommandPalette>` (:216).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/Shell.css` — the nav (:8–72), the rail media query `@media (max-width: 1099.98px)` (:75–86), the `.gm-shell.rail` rules (:88–98), the palette (:111–136).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/focus.ts` (whole file, 59 lines) — `useFocusTrap(ref, open, onEscape)`: on open focuses `[data-autofocus]` or the first focusable in `ref`, keeps Tab inside, calls `onEscape` on Escape (document capture listener), and on close focuses the element that was focused when it opened.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/Drawer.tsx` (lines 25–44) — the right-side drawer using `useFocusTrap`; the pattern to mirror for trap + overlay.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/base.css` (lines 184–197) — the generic `.drawer` class: `position: fixed; top: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; z-index: 41; width: 360px; max-width: 100%; border-left; animation: gm-slide-in` and `@media (max-width: 900px) { .drawer { width: 100%; } }`. `.gm-nav.drawer` inherits all of it and must override the right-side bits (see GOTCHA).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Terminals.tsx` (lines 449–494) and `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Terminals.css` (lines 202–207) — the existing Terminals sidebar drawer below 900 px: the pattern to mirror (scrim + `.drawer` class + `width: min(300px, 86vw)` + a toggle button with `aria-expanded`). Read only, don't change it.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/CommandPalette.tsx` (lines 106–110 `open()`, 127–178 render) — each `role="option"` row already has `onClick={() => open(item)}` (line 163); the overlay closes on `onMouseDown` on itself (line 129).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/Icon.tsx` — icons `menu` (line 98), `logo`, `close` exist.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/Shell.test.tsx` (whole file, 277 lines) — `renderShell(path)` (:71–85), fetch stub (:30–47), `afterEach` with `vi.unstubAllGlobals()` (:49–54), `loaded()` (:89–93). The existing tests run without `matchMedia` (desktop) and must keep passing unchanged; e.g. :96–108 expects `className` to be exactly `"gm-shell rail"` / `"gm-shell"`, and :127–143 counts the `.nav-item` links and the `Jump to…` button.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/App.tsx` (lines 66–85) — the routes and their page names: `/runs`, `/runs/:ws/:runId`, `/terminals`, `/workspaces`, `/projects`, `/reviewers`, `/settings`.

## Patterns to follow

**Terminals sidebar drawer (pages/Terminals.tsx:449-454, 483-488):**
```tsx
{(!narrow || drawer) && (
  <>
    {narrow && <div className="tsb-scrim" onClick={() => setDrawer(false)} aria-hidden="true" />}
    <TerminalSidebar className={narrow ? "drawer" : ""} … />
  </>
)}
…
<button type="button" className="btn btn-sm" aria-expanded={drawer} onClick={() => setDrawer((d) => !d)} data-testid="sidebar-toggle">
  <Icon name="menu" size={14} />
```
```css
/* pages/Terminals.css:206-207 */
.tsb.drawer { position: absolute; z-index: 15; top: 0; bottom: 0; left: 0; width: min(300px, 86vw); box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
.tsb-scrim { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 14; background: var(--overlay); }
```

**Focus trap (ui/Drawer.tsx:25-27):**
```tsx
const ref = useRef<HTMLElement>(null);
useFocusTrap(ref, open, onClose);
```

**Testing with a stubbed matchMedia:** jsdom has no `window.matchMedia`, so `useMedia(NARROW)` is `false` in every existing test (desktop). To test the phone layout, stub it so only the narrow query matches (theme's `prefers-color-scheme` query then reads `false`, which is fine):
```typescript
import { NARROW } from "./ui/media";

function stubNarrow(matching: string[] = [NARROW]) {
  vi.stubGlobal(
    "matchMedia",
    vi.fn((q: string) => ({ matches: matching.includes(q), media: q, addEventListener: vi.fn(), removeEventListener: vi.fn(), addListener: vi.fn(), removeListener: vi.fn() })),
  );
}
```
The file's existing `afterEach` already calls `vi.unstubAllGlobals()` (Shell.test.tsx:53). CSS isn't applied in vitest (no `css` option), so assert on DOM, classes and attributes, not on visibility.

## Step-by-step tasks

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/Shell.tsx`

- **IMPLEMENT**:
  1. Imports: add `import { NARROW, useMedia } from "./ui/media";` and `import { useFocusTrap } from "./ui/focus";`. `Link`, `useLocation`, `useRef`, `useCallback` are already imported.
  2. Export a pure helper next to `isLiveRunDetail`:
     ```typescript
     const PAGE_TITLES: Record<string, string> = { runs: "Runs", terminals: "Terminals", workspaces: "Workspaces", projects: "Projects", reviewers: "Reviewers", settings: "Settings" };

     /** The top bar title: the page name, or the run id on a run page. */
     export function pageTitle(pathname: string): string {
       const m = RUN_DETAIL.exec(pathname);
       if (m) return decodeURIComponent(m[2]!);
       return PAGE_TITLES[pathname.split("/")[1] ?? ""] ?? "graph-manager";
     }
     ```
  3. Inside `Shell` (after the existing state):
     ```typescript
     const narrow = useMedia(NARROW);
     const [navOpen, setNavOpen] = useState(false);
     const drawerOpen = narrow && navOpen;
     const navRef = useRef<HTMLElement>(null);
     const menuRef = useRef<HTMLButtonElement>(null);
     const closeNav = useCallback(() => setNavOpen(false), []);
     useFocusTrap(navRef, drawerOpen, closeNav);
     // Back to ☰ on close. iOS doesn't focus a tapped button, so the trap's own "focus the opener" isn't enough.
     const wasOpen = useRef(false);
     useEffect(() => {
       if (wasOpen.current && !drawerOpen && narrow && !palette) menuRef.current?.focus();
       wasOpen.current = drawerOpen;
     }, [drawerOpen, narrow, palette]);
     // A route change (a nav link tap) closes it; so does growing past 900 px.
     useEffect(() => { setNavOpen(false); }, [pathname]);
     useEffect(() => { if (!narrow) setNavOpen(false); }, [narrow]);
     ```
     Get `search` too if you want query-only changes (`/runs?status=live` from a status row while on `/runs`) to close it: use `const { pathname, search } = useLocation();` and `[pathname, search]`. Also add an `onClick` on the `<nav>` that closes the drawer when the click target is inside an `<a>` (`(e.target as Element).closest("a")`), so tapping the link of the page you're already on closes it too.
  4. The "Jump to…" button (:191) becomes `onClick={() => { setNavOpen(false); setPalette(true); }}` so the palette never opens under the drawer (two focus traps).
  5. Render, inside `<div className={rail ? "gm-shell rail" : "gm-shell"} …>` (keep that className expression unchanged), before `<nav>`:
     ```tsx
     {narrow && (
       <header className="gm-topbar" data-testid="gm-topbar">
         <button ref={menuRef} type="button" className="gm-topbar-menu" aria-label="Open navigation" aria-expanded={drawerOpen} aria-controls="gm-nav" data-testid="nav-menu" onClick={() => setNavOpen(true)}>
           <Icon name="menu" size={18} />
         </button>
         <span className="gm-topbar-brand" aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="logo" size={20} /></span>
         <span className="gm-topbar-title" data-testid="topbar-title">{pageTitle(pathname)}</span>
         {c.live > 0 && (
           <Link to="/runs?status=live" className="gm-topbar-live" aria-label={`${c.live} ${c.live === 1 ? "run" : "runs"} live`} data-testid="topbar-live">
             <span className="glyph glyph-pulse tone-live" aria-hidden="true" />
           </Link>
         )}
       </header>
     )}
     {drawerOpen && <div className="gm-nav-scrim" data-testid="nav-scrim" onClick={closeNav} aria-hidden="true" />}
     ```
     and the nav becomes `<nav ref={navRef} id="gm-nav" className={drawerOpen ? "gm-nav drawer" : "gm-nav"} aria-label="Main" tabIndex={-1} onClick={…}>` with the same children as today.
- **PATTERN**: `pages/Terminals.tsx:449-494` (scrim + drawer class + toggle with `aria-expanded`), `ui/Drawer.tsx:25-27` (focus trap).
- **GOTCHA**:
  - Don't render a second `.nav-item` link or a second "Jump to…" button in the top bar: Shell.test.tsx:127–143 counts them.
  - The nav stays in the DOM when closed on a phone (CSS hides it), so its counts and badges keep updating and nothing remounts.
  - Effect order: React runs all cleanups before all new effect bodies, so the trap's cleanup (focus the opener) runs first and the "focus ☰" effect wins; it skips when the palette just opened, because the palette's own trap must keep focus in its input.
  - `useFocusTrap` handles Escape on a `document` capture listener. Shell's window capture keydown (:98–130) ignores Escape, so nothing else needs to change for it.
  - The top bar title on the live run page is the run id too (below 900 px the live run page uses the top bar like every other page).
- **VALIDATE**: `cd apps/graph-manager && npx vitest run src/web/Shell.test.tsx`

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/Shell.css`

- **IMPLEMENT**:
  1. Change the rail query on line 75 from `@media (max-width: 1099.98px)` to `@media (min-width: 900px) and (max-width: 1099.98px)`, so the drawer below 900 px shows full labels.
  2. Wrap the ten `.gm-shell.rail …` rules (:89–98) in `@media (min-width: 900px) { … }`.
  3. Fix the header comment on line 1 to mention the phone top bar.
  4. Append:
     ```css
     /* Phones (below 900px): a 48px top bar with ☰; the nav opens as a drawer from the left. */
     .gm-topbar { display: none; }
     @keyframes gm-slide-in-left { from { transform: translateX(-24px); opacity: 0; } }
     @media (max-width: 899.98px) {
       .gm-shell { flex-direction: column; }
       .gm-main { flex: 1 1 0; height: auto; min-height: 0; }
       .gm-nav:not(.drawer) { display: none; }
       .gm-topbar {
         display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; height: 48px; flex: 0 0 auto; padding: 0 8px 0 4px;
         background: var(--sf); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bd); color: var(--fg); font-size: 14px;
       }
       .gm-topbar-menu, .gm-topbar-live {
         width: 40px; height: 40px; flex: 0 0 auto; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
         padding: 0; border: 0; border-radius: 6px; background: transparent; color: var(--fg2); cursor: pointer;
       }
       .gm-topbar-menu:hover { background: var(--sf2); color: var(--fg); }
       .gm-topbar-brand { display: inline-flex; flex: 0 0 auto; }
       .gm-topbar-title { flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 0; font-weight: 500; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
       .gm-nav.drawer {
         position: fixed; top: 0; bottom: 0; left: 0; right: auto; z-index: 41; height: auto;
         width: min(300px, 86vw); max-width: none; border-left: 0; border-right: 1px solid var(--bd); box-shadow: var(--shadow);
         padding: calc(14px + env(safe-area-inset-top)) 10px calc(14px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom)) calc(10px + env(safe-area-inset-left));
         animation: gm-slide-in-left var(--dur-base) ease-out;
       }
       .gm-nav-scrim { position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 40; background: var(--overlay); animation: gm-fade var(--dur-fast) ease-out; }
       html.kb-open .gm-topbar { display: none; }
       /* Command palette on a phone */
       .palette-overlay { padding: calc(48px + env(safe-area-inset-top)) 0 0; }
       .palette { width: calc(100% - 16px); max-width: none; max-height: calc(var(--app-h, 100dvh) - 96px); }
     }
     @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .gm-nav.drawer, .gm-nav-scrim { animation: none; } }
     ```
- **GOTCHA**: `.gm-nav.drawer` also matches the generic `.drawer` in `ui/base.css:185-189,194` (`right: 0; width: 360px; border-left; gm-slide-in` from the right; `width: 100%` under 900 px). `.gm-nav.drawer` (two classes) beats `.drawer` (one class), so every one of those properties must be overridden above: `right: auto`, `width`, `max-width: none`, `border-left: 0`, the left-side animation. Also override `.gm-nav`'s own `position: sticky` and `height` (from line 9). Palette z-index is 55 and toasts 60, both above the drawer (41) and scrim (40).
- **VALIDATE**: `npm run lint`

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/CommandPalette.tsx`

- **IMPLEMENT**: keep the existing `onClick={() => open(item)}` on every `role="option"` row (line 163) — it is what makes a tap work — and keep the keyboard behaviour (ArrowUp/Down, Ctrl+j/k/n/p, Enter, Escape through `useFocusTrap`) unchanged. No other change is required here; the narrow sizing is CSS (above). If you touch the file, don't replace `onClick` with mouse-only handlers.
- **VALIDATE**: `cd apps/graph-manager && npx vitest run src/web/Shell.test.tsx`

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/Shell.test.tsx`

- **IMPLEMENT**: add `import { NARROW } from "./ui/media";`, `import { pageTitle } from "./Shell";` (extend the existing import), the `stubNarrow()` helper shown above, and a `describe("Shell on a phone", …)` with:
  1. "shows the top bar with ☰, the brand and the page title below 900 px": `stubNarrow(); renderShell("/workspaces"); await loaded();` → `getByTestId("gm-topbar")` exists, `getByTestId("nav-menu")` has `aria-label="Open navigation"` and `aria-expanded="false"`, `getByTestId("topbar-title").textContent === "Workspaces"`, `getByTestId("topbar-live")` exists (one live run in the fixture), `queryByTestId("nav-scrim")` is null, and the `<nav aria-label="Main">` has no `drawer` class.
  2. "opens the nav drawer and a nav link closes it": click `nav-menu` → `aria-expanded="true"`, `screen.getByRole("navigation", { name: "Main" }).className` contains `drawer`, `nav-scrim` exists, `document.activeElement` is inside the nav. Click the `Projects` link (`getByRole("link", { name: "Projects" })`) → `where() === "/projects"`, no `nav-scrim`, `aria-expanded="false"`, `document.activeElement === getByTestId("nav-menu")`.
  3. "the scrim closes it": open, `fireEvent.click(getByTestId("nav-scrim"))` → closed, focus on `nav-menu`.
  4. "Escape closes it": open, `fireEvent.keyDown(document.activeElement!, { key: "Escape" })` → closed.
  5. "Jump to closes the drawer and opens the palette, and a tap on an item navigates": open, click `Jump to…`, the palette (`getByTestId("palette")`) is open and `nav-scrim` gone; type `"Reviewers"` into the combobox and `fireEvent.click(screen.getAllByRole("option")[0]!)` → `where() === "/reviewers"`.
  6. "has no top bar on a desktop": no stub → `queryByTestId("gm-topbar")` is null (the existing desktop tests cover the rest).
  7. `pageTitle`: `/runs` → `Runs`, `/terminals` → `Terminals`, `/settings` → `Settings`, `/runs/github~o~r/20261106-193934-b2dc` → `20261106-193934-b2dc`, `/nope` → `graph-manager`.
- **GOTCHA**: `fireEvent.click` doesn't focus the button in jsdom, which is exactly the iOS case the explicit "focus ☰" effect covers. Wrap interactions in `act` only if React warns; `fireEvent` already does.
- **VALIDATE**: `cd apps/graph-manager && npx vitest run src/web/Shell.test.tsx`

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Below 900 px there is no nav or rail in the page flow; `gm-topbar` (48 px) shows ☰ (`nav-menu`, `aria-label="Open navigation"`, `aria-expanded`), the brand, the page title (Runs, Terminals, Workspaces, Projects, Reviewers, Settings, or the run id on a run page) and a live-runs dot linking to `/runs?status=live` when runs are live.
- [ ] Tapping ☰ opens the full nav (labels, badges, status rows, Jump to, theme, Log out) as `.gm-nav.drawer` from the left, `width: min(300px, 86vw)`, over `.gm-nav-scrim`; focus moves into it.
- [ ] A nav link tap (route change), a scrim tap and Escape each close it, and focus returns to ☰. Jump to… closes it and opens the palette.
- [ ] From 900 to 1099 px the 56 px rail is unchanged; from 1100 px up the full nav is unchanged; `.gm-shell.rail` (live run detail) only takes effect at 900 px and up. No `gm-topbar` at 900 px and up.
- [ ] `html.kb-open` hides `gm-topbar` below 900 px.
- [ ] The palette is `calc(100% - 16px)` wide and at most `calc(var(--app-h, 100dvh) - 96px)` tall below 900 px; a tap (click) on an item navigates; keyboard behaviour is unchanged.
- [ ] Every existing `Shell.test.tsx` test passes unchanged, plus the new phone tests.
- [ ] Tests pass: `cd apps/graph-manager && npx vitest run src/web/Shell.test.tsx`

## Validation commands

```bash
# Type / lint (repo root)
npm run typecheck && npm run lint

# Tests for this slice
cd apps/graph-manager && npx vitest run src/web/Shell.test.tsx src/web/ui

# Whole suite (repo root)
npm test
```
Known environment failure: `packages/graph-execution/src/cli.test.ts` "exits 2 at startup when --provider claude is not on the PATH" fails where a real `claude` binary is installed next to `node`; ignore only that one.
